   "claims": [
    "To calculate the markup as a percentage, you use the following formula: markup percentage = revenue – cost / cost × 100% So, to express the markup as a percentage, simply multiply it by 100%.",
    "Suppose it costs a company $100 to produce a widget and, using the cost-plus pricing model, the company wants to sell that widget with a 25% markup.",
    "In order to determine the final price, you will then need to use the following formula: price = cost × (1 + markup) For example, let’s calculate the cost-plus pricing for a markup of 0.25."
   ],
